The Witness Freshness Rule is a mountain legal standard: route records older than one active season are treated as rumor until re-witnessed.
It emerged from volcanic pass dynamics where maps became obsolete faster than civic ledgers could update.
The rule spread from route-house practice into broader logistics law, influencing coastal and archival authenticity standards.
Its core thesis is that safety-critical truth expires without current witness renewal.
